### THE FOCUS-STEALING DIAGNOSIS — do not re-investigate

The Prose codebase is NOT the cause. Every `ProcessStartInfo` in v3 already sets
`CreateNoWindow = true`. The Launcher's two `UseShellExecute` spawns are a URL and WinExe apps.
The Hub's console is deliberate.

**It is `MindAttic.Automata.Tick`** — `automata-runner.exe tick`, repeat `PT5M`, principal
`LogonType = Interactive`, so it runs on the desktop and its console takes focus every 5 minutes.
`MindAtticBobNightlyBackup` is already `S4U` on the same machine and never flashes — that is both
the proof and the shape of the fix.

Also Interactive (daily, less noticeable): `ProseAutoCorrectNightly` (03:00),
`StreetSamurai-NightlyFactSweep` (01:00 — **its last run exited 1; it has been failing nightly**).

`Set-ScheduledTask` returned **Access is denied** from this session — it needs elevation.

