## HARD gotchas (do not rediscover)

- **The author redeploys, not me.** A local build changes nothing.
- **Do not stage the author's 8 files:** `ObligationCli.cs`, `BeatGeneratorService.cs`,
  `ProseWriterRouter.cs`, `v4/Prose.V4.Cli/Program.cs` (they have ~351 lines of unfinished
  `beat-history` work in it — I staged ONLY my one `using` line via `git hash-object` +
  `git update-index --cacheinfo`), `docs/rfc/0013`, 3 `.prose/` files.
- **`.ps1` files MUST be written UTF-8 WITH BOM.** PS 5.1 decodes a BOM-less script as ANSI and
  mangles every em dash. Hit and fixed this session.
- **Razor: `@page.Text` in markup parses as the `@page` directive** — name the variable anything
  else. **`@{ }` inside an existing code block is a parse error.** **`@ref` needs an assignable
  location** (`array[i]`, not a dictionary).
- **`BeatEntityPresence` has no EF mapping** — it does not exist on SQLite, so `BlastRadiusService`
  throws there. `CarriedByAsync` isolates it and reports reach as UNKNOWN, never zero.
- **`ef migrations add` needs `--startup-project Prose.Core --context ProseDbContext`** — using
  `Prose.Cli` as startup tries to reach the Hub and fails.
- **`prose.cmd` + a heredoc in one Bash call DEADLOCKS.** Always `< /dev/null`.
- **Every book-touching method must `SetFlowUniverse` first.**
- The 5 failing tests are pre-existing. Leave them.
